{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "stress_divergence_strintx",
    "description": "B-grid lowering rule of the internal-stress x-divergence rewrite target strintx = D(sigma11, x) + D(sigma12, y), the momentum-equation divergence of the internal stress tensor: the Fortran assembles it at each U point as strintx(i,j) = uarear(i,j)*(str(i,j,1) + str(i+1,j,2) + str(i,j+1,3) + str(i+1,j+1,4)) (stepu, ice_dyn_shared.F90:958-959) from the str corner combinations of the stress() routine (ice_dyn_evp.F90:1727-1743). The rule matches the two-term sum by GROUND PATTERN (sigma11/sigma12 literal, so no where-shape constraint is possible or needed, esm-spec 9.6.1/9.6.8) and emits the [i,j] makearray of the four surrounding-cell corner contributions tiled over four i/j position classes (interior [1..N_I-1]x[1..N_J-1], the i = N_I strip, the j = N_J strip, and the (N_I,N_J) corner) with halo-copy closures: on the i = N_I strip the cells (i+1,j) and (i+1,j+1) that supply the k2/k4 str atoms are replaced by (N_I,j)/(N_I,j+1), and on the j = N_J strip the cells (i,j+1) and (i+1,j+1) by (i,N_J)/(i+1,N_J) (the ghost-cell stress copies the edge value, as the Fortran's ice_HaloUpdate of the stress arrays does before stress()). Each region value is a faq over its box that applies the four scalar str atoms str_dx_cell_k1..k4, each bound to its own cell's corner stresses and metrics: the p_k = sigma11 + sigma22, m_k = sigma11 - sigma22, s_k = sigma12 corner combinations (the stressp/stressm/stress12 of the stress() routine, F90:1667-1686) and the cell's dxT/dyT/dxhy/dyhx (ice_dyn_evp.F90:410-416), the whole sum scaled by uarear(i,j), the U-cell inverse area (ice_grid.F90:703). Requires N_I >= 2 and N_J >= 2.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:cice_bgrid",
      "grid:cice_bgrid",
      "op:D",
      "axes:i,j",
      "order:1",
      "bc:halo-copy",
      "stagger:b",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hunke, E. C., et al. (2023). CICE v6.3.22 documentation and user's guide (LA-UR-23-31851), the EVP dynamics stress and stepu."
      }
    ]
  },
